## Arrays — DSA Revision Notes

**Pattern:**

* Traverse the array using a loop
* Compare elements
* Track a variable such as `max`, `min`, `sum`, `count`, or `index`
* Use two pointers when working from both ends
* Use prefix sum for repeated range-sum calculations
* Use hashing when you need fast lookup/frequency counting

**When to use:**

* Finding maximum/minimum element
* Searching for an element
* Counting elements/frequencies
* Finding duplicates
* Finding pairs/subarrays
* Rearranging elements
* Calculating sums
* Problems involving contiguous elements
* When the input is a collection of values stored in order

**Important template:**

Basic traversal:

```java
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    // process arr[i]
}
```

Find maximum:

```java
int max = arr[0];

for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] > max) {
        max = arr[i];
    }
}
```

Two-pointer array:

```java
int left = 0;
int right = arr.length - 1;

while (left < right) {
    // process arr[left] and arr[right]

    left++;
    right--;
}
```

**Common mistakes:**

* Using `i <= arr.length` instead of `i < arr.length`
* Accessing `arr[i + 1]` when `i` is the last index
* Accessing `arr[i - 1]` when `i == 0`
* Forgetting to handle an empty array
* Incorrectly initializing `max`/`min`
* Modifying the array when it is not required
* Confusing **index** with **value**
* Using nested loops when an `O(n)` solution is possible
* Forgetting that array indexing starts from `0`

